# ==========================================================
# PHASE D — BACKEND ARCHITECTURE (CURRENT PHASE)
# ==========================================================

IMPORTANT

Phase A (Product Planning),
Phase B (Design System),
and Phase C (Frontend Prototype)
are already completed and approved.

DO NOT redesign or rebuild any frontend.

DO NOT modify UI unless backend integration requires a very small adjustment.

Your responsibility now is to design a production-ready backend architecture that will gradually replace the current mock layer.

The backend must remain fully compatible with the existing Next.js frontend.

Every backend module should expose interfaces that match the current mock data structure to minimize frontend refactoring.

Use:

- NestJS
- GraphQL (Apollo)
- PostgreSQL
- Prisma ORM
- Redis
- BullMQ
- Firebase Cloud Messaging
- WebSocket
- JWT Authentication
- Refresh Tokens
- Docker
- Object Storage (S3 Compatible)

Use Clean Architecture + Modular Monolith.

Every module must be independently maintainable.

Avoid tightly coupled business logic.

